WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.730
It was just a crazy idea.

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.770
I was sitting on a plane and it was dark outside

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.370
and I was thinking crazy.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.170
If I were a vampire, I had to get myself a ticket for a night flight

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:15.770
and when this gets hijacked, I have a serious problem.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.210
When I write the story, I'm just thinking,

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.270
"Okay, what do I think is cool?

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.570
What do I like?"

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:28.970
I was thinking maybe we should do it much more emotional,

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.050
and then I came up with the idea that

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.350
she is not alone on the board.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.570
She has a little boy.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.010
So we added this to the story

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.290
and this is what really makes it special.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.890
I think it's easy to connect with her because she's a mother

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.330
and there's the son.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:48.100
I think even if you don't have children of your own,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.410
I think this is something everyone can relate to.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.510
We have the framed story,

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:56.970
the movie begins with the end.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:01.890
First she definitely is the main character, but switches to the boy.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.890
I never believed that Blood Red Sky was just working in Germany,

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.730
so it shouldn't be a German movie.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:15.010
And I had the idea what can be more international

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.170
than a transatlantic flight.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.570
When it comes to writing, I cannot stop it.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:27.130
I think it can be quite frustrating for all the people around me,

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.170
especially my wife and my son.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.930
When it flows and you have an idea it's great, 

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:35.530
but it can also be very very frustrating if you get

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:38.730
writers block and don't know how to go on.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:46.450
The most difficult part was doing this action sequences because

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:51.910
it takes place in a very contained environment.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:52.690
How can we do it?

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:57.790
Because our main guy is over here in the front of the plane

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.730
and the other one is at the back of the plane,

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.370
and it was like playing chess.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:05.410
Thank you very much.

